<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=Edge">
<meta name="viewport"
	content="initial-scale=1.0, width=device-width, viewport-fit=cover">
<title>404 - Page not found - Met Office</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/public/error-pages/http-errors.css"
	type="text/css" />
</head>
<body>
	<div class="http-error">
		<img class="error-image" src="/public/error-pages/umbrella_trans.png"
			alt="broken umbrella">
		<div class="error-content">
			<img class="mo-logo" src="/public/error-pages/mo-logo-black.svg"
				alt="metoffice-logo">
			<h1>We can't find the page you were looking for</h1>
			<p>The link you followed may be broken or the page removed.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="error-detail">
			<hr />
			<h2>Here are some options to help:</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>Check the address is entered as you expected</li>
				<li>Visit our <a href="/">homepage</a> to discover more about
					what we do
				</li>
				<li>Try searching the Met Office website for information<br />
					<form action="/search">
						<input placeholder="Search Met Office" name="query" />
						<button type="submit">Go</button>
					</form>
				</li>
				<li>Believe this to be an error or still having an issue? <a
					href="/about-us/contact">Contact us</a></li>
			</ul>
			<hr />
			www.metoffice.gov.uk <a href="/about-us/legal#licences"
				class="copyright">&copy; Crown copyright</a>
		</div>
	</div>
</body>
</html>